## 5. School services

The Software is not an official product of Institute of Science Tokyo and is
not endorsed by it. It connects to university systems (such as the
portal, LMS and course registration) using your own account. You are
responsible for using those systems in line with the university's rules. The
university may change or block access at any time, and features that depend
on it may stop working.

## 6. Your data

The Software stores your data on your device. Sign-in credentials are kept in
your operating system's credential store. If you turn on cloud backup, a copy
is saved in your own cloud account (for example, Google Drive). The Software
downloads public reference data, such as academic calendars, from our data
repository. School requests go to the school services; enabled backups go to your own
Google Drive or OneDrive account. Public data requests reach GitHub, whose
service may log connection metadata such as your IP address. This release
does not include usage analytics or a developer-operated workspace server.
Keep backups of important records and confirm dates in official sources.

